WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.240
"Pewdiepie was always kinda racist - but now he's a hero to the Nazis"

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.060
Wait a minute.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:08.980
No!

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.080
You changed it!?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:10.840
Come on, media.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.460
What are you doing?

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.280
What does it say now?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.220
"Pewdiepie's fall shows the limits of 'Lol Just Kidding'"!

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:17.980
Hey

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.620
Alright

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.740
"Emma Grey Ellis"

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.340
May I just say that:

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.540
If you're gonna call someone

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.560
"a hero to the Nazis",

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.760
you may wanna double-check if that's true or not.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.160
Because afterwards you can't go "Lawl just kidding".

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.860
The amount of cherry-picking that the media came out with after this whole thing to prove this narrative that I am somehow

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.580
That was ...

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:42.800
... beautiful.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.900
Please keep doing it. It's hilarious.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.260
Vox media posted this un-ironically

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:59.880
"Arguably similar to nazi fashion: recently he has been wearing Himmler style glasses and sporting a fashy (slang for fascist) Hitler youth haircut."

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.680
Vox.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.980
You got me.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:04.840
Damn it.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.480
I didn't want to admit this.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.500
I didn't wanna talk about this.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.060
I love Korean fashion.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.960
I love K-Pop. That's why I dyed my hair.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.040
I'm going through a mid-life crisis here, okay?

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.800
I wanna be a K-Pop star.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.260
J.K. Rowling is calling me a fascist. I don't... Why? I don't...

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.620
I guess she read it on a... She read it off a headline...

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.520
And sorta went with it

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.440
Well...

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.400
I read on an online article

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.400
that you once said in an interview that you found dressing up as a Nazi arousing.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.840
I read that on an online website, so it must be true.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:49.840
Right?

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:50.440
J.K.?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.020
So..

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:58.200
I made the apology video where, I thought at least, was from the heart explained the situation

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.500
And I admitted that I didn't do everything-

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.120
Like, I'm not guilt-free in this situation by any means.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:09.700
It was... It was met by... just the warmest positivity from the Internet.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:16.880
An... And anyone that I think saw it... It was just amazing and I owe you guys my biggest thanks for all the support that I got from that video.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:17.860
However,

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.860
the media wasn't as impressed.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.060
They- they kinda stuck with their narrative.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.400
"Pewdiepie half-heartedly apologizes, calls media 'motherfuckers'"

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:34.020
"Pewdiepie's 'apology' for Nazi jokes shows that he still doesn't get it"

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.080
"Trump and Pewdiepie are using the same playbook"

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.540
So we basically went from "Pewdiepie is a nazi" to "Pewdiepie is Trump".

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.740
We'll get there one day, Media.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.320
I'm sure we'll get there one day.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.440
And I wanna point out,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.580
not all media.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.080
Okay?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.540
I've seen more and more balanced articles come out about this situation.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.240
Even though it seems pretty dead at this point.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.540
The whole situation, this is a testimony of old media not understanding YouTube.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:04.040
The fucking senior editor of Wall Street Journal *laughs*...

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.360
The senior editor of WSJ tweeted:

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.880
"Man, this Pewdiepie video is looooong."

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:16.640
I'm..I'm sorry, Mike. I'll try and cut it down next time a little bit for you, so you don't have to spend so much time.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.180
Doing your ... Journalist research,

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.140
I'll.. Maybe I'll add a little meme.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.660
I'll add a little meme.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.020
Maybe that will make it more interesting for you.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:27.820
I don't... I don't know...

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.100
Senior editor, huh?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.080
How about that...

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.080
Let's get into the Wall Street Journal thing.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.800
There's one thing that I wanted to talk about,

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.260
that I didn't really do in my last video, which was

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.760
the fact that Wall Street Journal

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.720
went to the brands

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.660
that I work with

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.580
before they came to me

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.640
for a comment.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.820
I know this because they didn't just talk to Disney and YouTube.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.380
It shows to me

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.620
that they were just after making the strongest headline

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.280
and the strongest story that they could get

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.040
without any regards of what kind of damage they would do

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.200
in the process.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.380
I mean, why...

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.100
why would Wall Street Journal care about minimizing harm?

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.040
It's not like it's one of the four major sections in the journalism code of ethics.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.220
I... I... I.. I

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.240
I mean, why would Wall Street Journal care about that?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.320
I don't understand.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.940
They wanted that headline - they got the headline.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:20.760
"Wall Street Journal should've tried to get a response from me directly to begin with. Not going to brands I work with first. Proves to me their maliciousness"

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.120
Christopher Mims of the Wall Street Journal tweeted back at me:

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.460
"Demonstrably false, but anyway welcome to our post-truth age."

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:35.840
He says: "nothing -- absolutely nothing -- gets printed in the Wall Street Journal without an attempt to reach a mentioned subject for comment".

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:36.720
So,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.480
Seems fair, right?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.900
But then he goes and says:

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.520
"I have no idea about the chronology."

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.680
Which was my fucking point!

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:45.220
Christopher Mims,

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.500
You demonstrated yourself false.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.760
So, welcome to the post-truth age.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.440
The other thing that I had a problem with, which I already brought up...

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.580
I don't.. I don't think I need to elaborate on it.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.040
Which is ... the context,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.440
or lack of context,

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.400
I think in the video there was one piece of context

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.800
out of five in total.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.300
So...

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.920
If you think that's a balanced way of doing journalism,

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:05.640
you tell me.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.840
I have a big problem with the whole thing in general

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.460
because,

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.520
this whole thing wasn't a problem until it was brought up.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.000
Because my audience understands they were jokes.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.860
They weren't actually doing anyone any harm.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.080
But the way the Wall Street Journal defended this was

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.960
that neo nazi web sites were supporting me.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.320
Calling it "the #1 Pewdiepie fan-site".

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.100
Which I obviously had no idea about.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:28.720
I don't,

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:29.560
Believe it or not,

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.420
I don't go to neo-nazi websites.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.860
The Wall Street Journal condemns me for using

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:35.940
"posts".

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.780
They don't call it jokes.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.960
They literally said

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:39.460
that

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.160
the fact that I used Adolf Hitler

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.240
and the fact that I used Nazi imagery;

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.100
that's bad enough.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:46.440
It seems,

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.260
right here,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.440
that you are guilty

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:49.880
of the same thing.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.080
Oh, look!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.040
There is Hitler!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.260
This looks like Nazi imagery to me!

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.340
Someone start the press!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.140
I think we have a "scoop"!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.820
It turns out the neo-nazi website have changed their mind.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.780
Right now they are the #1 Wall Street Journal fan-site!

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.340
Interesting!

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.220
I don't believe Wall Street Journal has made a statement,

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.820
condemning these websites.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:19.160
So they must be a Nazi-supporting website now.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.840
I think we need to talk to their sponsors about this.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.700
NOT Wall Street Journal themselves.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.800
Or does context matter?

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.940
I don't know.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:29.680
Oh, look!

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.400
Here's their sponsors!

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.040
How about that?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.380
Guess we need to talk to them first.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.740
I realize how childish I sound.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.320
Okay?

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.480
It's just to illustrate this point.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.080
And if you didn't think it could be any more unethical,

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.560
or any more stupid:

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.580
One of their journalists,

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.220
Ben Fritz,

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.760
it came out that he's been doing the same kind of jokes.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:52.800
No!

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.080
Not Ben Fritz!

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.120
Say it's not true!

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:59.680
He has a hard on for the Nazis.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:00.500
No!

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.460
NOO!

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.340
That's an anti-semetic joke!

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.940
He wants to fry the jews?

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:10.540
I don't even... Sorry... Sorry... I-I don't even want to show these jokes.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:14.340
I don't show anti-semetic imagery on my channel. That's disgusting.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.540
I'm so disappointed in you, Ben Fritz.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.760
I didn't wanna say this,

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.300
because it didn't feel necessary,

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.100
but there wasn't just pressure to get my show cancelled.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.200
Along with other brands that I worked with that they reached out to,

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:30.240
YouTube also had pressure to demonetize my entire channel.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.140
Essentially, getting me fired.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:36.180
Luckily, my videos does not go against community guidelines.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:36.800
So it didn't.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.000
But they tried.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.700
So it seems only fair,

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.800
by Wall Street Journal's own way of conducting themselves, that Ben Fritz

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:45.940
should get fired.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.860
This whole thing has been embarrassing.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:50.700
It's been a fiasco.

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:54.700
It doesn't make me happy when I find... like, these things out. It makes me sad.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.200
...That this is the world we live in.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.440
Where people...

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.120
People make articles about people making jokes,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.300
that they make themselves.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.120
Trying to get their lives ruined.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.280
A thing that I saw a lot on the media was that,

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.080
because I said,

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.400
"Wall Street Journal did this attack on me",

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.560
and people just didn't believe me, like:

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.500
"What does Wall Street Journal has to gain from that?" or,

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:20.040
"They're such a different organization, like, they have nothing to do with what I do, so it wouldn't make any sense".

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:25.280
Well, here's a graph showing the trust in media going down based on age.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.080
I assume that pieces like this is not helping with that.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:35.720
Here's a graph of the newspaper ad revenue from digital and print, showing decrease of revenue in the media.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:40.480
Oh, okay, so Wall Street is losing influence and income...

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.700
Hmm, I wonder who's gaining that right now?

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:48.140
So what does Wall Street Journal has to gain from doing a piece like this on me?

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:48.740
Nothing!

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:49.800
Nothing, obviously.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:54.320
I mean, why else would they put the article behind a pay-wall? Twice!

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.400
So Wall Street Journal is losing revenue.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:58.800
Maybe...

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.740
Maybe I should buy the Wall Street Journal?

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:03.560
Actually, I don't know.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.100
Seems like a failing business to me.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:32.100
*music plays*

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.760
*laughing*

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.300
Context matters, Ben!

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.300
*laughing*

